.TH DUI 8 2026-11-13 DarqOS "DarqOS System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
dui \- install or update DarqOS from a distribution tarball
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dui
.RB [ \-\-boot ]
.RB [ \-\-pre\-release ]
.RB [ \-\-update ]
.RI [ tarball ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dui
(DarqOS Updater/Installer) installs DarqOS from a distribution tarball
made by
.BR mkdist :
the
.I tarball
given, or the stable release, downloaded from GitHub, or, with
.BR \-\-pre\-release ,
the newest pre-release.
It is used both for the first install on a host and for later
updates, by hand, and by
.BR darqos\-update (8).
It must be run as root.
.PP
.B dui
performs these steps, stopping with an error if any fails:
.IP 1. 4
Without a
.IR tarball ,
download the release, and its signature, into
.I /tmp
with
.BR wget (1).
.IP 2.
Check the tarball's signature, beside it
.RI ( tarball .sig),
with the installed release key,
.IR /etc/darqos/allowed_signers ,
and say what it found.
Run by hand, it installs the tarball all the same, as it's asked, and
its release key with it: a manual install trusts the distribution it's
given.
.IP 3.
Remove any existing
.BR $DIST ,
and unpack the tarball into it, owned by root.
.IP 4.
Run
.BR $DIST/darq/bin/install ,
passing it
.B \-\-boot
and
.BR \-\-update .
.IP 5.
Remove
.BR $DIST .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-boot
Make DarqOS the machine's default boot: see
.BR install (8).
.TP
.B \-\-pre\-release
Without a
.IR tarball ,
download the newest pre-release, rather than the stable release:
pre-releases are for trying out, not for a system whose data can't be
lost.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Install as an update, which
.BR darqos\-update (8)
has checked: the release key isn't installed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DARQ
Installation root.
Default:
.IR /darq .
.TP
.B DIST
Staging directory for the unpacked distribution.
Default:
.BR $DARQ/dist .
.TP
.B CONF_DIR
Where the release key is installed.
Default:
.IR /etc/darqos .
.TP
.B DARQOS_STABLE
URL of the stable release's tarball.
Default:
.IR https://github.com/darqos/darqos/releases/latest/download/darqos.tar.gz .
.TP
.B DARQOS_RELEASES
URL of GitHub's list of releases, to find the newest pre-release.
Default:
.IR https://api.github.com/repos/darqos/darqos/releases .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/darqos.tar.gz
The downloaded tarball, with its signature,
.IR /tmp/darqos.tar.gz.sig .
They aren't removed afterwards.
.TP
.I /etc/darqos/allowed_signers
The installed release key.
.TP
.I $DIST/darq/bin/install
The install script run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if it installed; 1 if a step, or the install, failed; 2 for a bad
option.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Progress is written to standard output as lines starting
.RB \(lq Ok: \(rq,
or
.RB \(lq Warning: \(rq,
and errors to standard error as lines starting
.RB \(lq Error: \(rq.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR install (8),
.BR darqos\-update (8),
.BR ssh\-keygen (1),
.BR wget (1)
